{"entryId":"1590","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1590:1","sourceSha256":"c226690900fb0fb7dbf3d9eb274c96cfc8b2cc5978685333b67d393128f039ca","englishSha256":"9dd998e34e30dec88d902ea0cc9b295d68c7ffcbfdd0aa1c52bcadcb25925c85","citations":[{"id":"1590:1:citation-01","he":[16,50],"en":[44,55],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_39b.18"},"reference":"Chullin 39b:18","assessment":"Rav Tuvi bar Rav Mattana sent the question to Rav Yosef in the checked Chullin text. The extra Rav is a witness difference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 39b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_39b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1590:1:citation-02","he":[51,76],"en":[57,103],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_36b.12"},"reference":"Bava Kamma 36b:12","assessment":"The exact Bava Kamma text names Rav Tuvyah bar Mattana sending a question to Rav Yosef. Thus ב\"מ here expands the patronymic bar Mattana, with Bava Kamma as the cited tractate. Correct the English which creates a Bava Metzia citation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Kamma 36b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_36b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 39b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_39b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1590:1:citation-03","he":[78,118],"en":[122,136],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_58a.8"},"reference":"Bava Batra 58a:8","assessment":"Exact Chezkat HaBatim narrative in Bava Batra. The magus opened graves and was held by the beard. The comparison has Abaye coming and the release after cutting the beard. Avoid assuming that Heilprin supplies the instrument mentioned by the Bavli.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 58a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_58a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1590:1:citation-04","he":[263,305],"en":[415,430],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_151a.11"},"reference":"Bava Batra 151a:11","assessment":"The exact morning and evening transfer story names two brothers, followed by Rav Nachman’s appraisal. It gives no statement that the family consisted of only those two brothers.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 151a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_151a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1590:1:citation-05","he":[630,676],"en":[1113,1127],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_16a.13"},"reference":"Moed Katan 16a:13","assessment":"Moed Katan names Rav Tuvi bar Mattana as the person insulted and says Abaye and Rava imposed the ban on the butcher.","evidence":[{"reference":"Moed Katan 16a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_16a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1590:1:citation-06","he":[678,702],"en":[1178,1189],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Temurah_29a.2"},"reference":"Temurah 29a:2","assessment":"The direct wording makes Rav Tuvi bar Mattana the transmitter in Rabbi Yoshiyah’s name. The existing bare quotation can explicitly carry that transmission direction.","evidence":[{"reference":"Temurah 29a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Temurah_29a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"holds":[{"raw":"ונראה כי לרב מתנה זה לא היו לו רק ב' בנים אלו","reason":"The property story mentions two brothers and supplies no exhaustive family list. The other patronyms and chronological distinction remain the compiler’s argument.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 151a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_151a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2589:1","target":{"entry":2589,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"Verified the exact Bava Kamma locus and reversed the erroneous expansion of the patronymic as Bava Metzia. The direct Temurah passage supplies the direction of transmission. Preserve the distinct cave and property stories and the tentative restriction of the family to two brothers.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 39b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_39b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Kamma 36b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_36b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 58a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_58a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 151a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_151a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2588:1","target":{"entry":2588,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2589:1","target":{"entry":2589,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Moed Katan 16a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_16a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Temurah 29a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Temurah_29a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
